<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juliana of Stolberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1506">1506</a>–<a href="/years/1580">1580</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juliana of Stolberg was a German countess, daughter of Count Botho III of Stolberg, who married William, Count of Nassau-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dillenburg">Dillenburg</a>, in 1531. Of her many children, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-silent">William the Silent</a> led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a> and his brothers Louis, Adolf and Henry died in its cause, while John VI of Nassau-Dillenburg became a Calvinist leader. She is remembered as the mother of the house of Orange-Nassau.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juliana-of-stolberg.jpg" alt="Juliana of Stolberg" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portret_van_Juliana_van_Stolberg_(1506-1580).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
